                  "visibilityToleranceMeters": 1,
                  "maximumEmissionDegrees": 70,
                  "interpretation": "Trial acceptance bounds, not estimates of source accuracy. A footprint is the pixel's range times its angular size, 9.7 million kilometres at the disc centre from 162 parsecs, so a contributor lies within two of those of the closest sphere point; the one-metre visibility tolerance is numerically zero on a body this size, and the sphere is convex, so no point occludes another."
